==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro||*h₂h₁tro-h₃kʷs|having the appearance of fire}}, from {{m|ine-pro||*h₂eh₁tro-}}, {{l|en|thematicized}} form of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eh₁ter-||fire}} (whence {{m|la|āter}}), + {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-||eye; to see}} (whence {{m|la|oculus}}). The first root also gives the cognates {{cog|ae|𐬁𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬱||fire}}, {{cog|xum|𐌀𐌈𐌓𐌖}}, {{cog|osc|𐌀𐌀𐌃𐌝𐌓𐌉𐌉𐌔}}, {{cog|ga|áith||kiln}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|atrōx}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|atrōx|comp=atrōcior|sup=atrōcissimus|adv=atrōciter}}

